fety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":32,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"All deliverables are in place. Summary:\n\n**What I changed and why.** The trained network switches at the first allowed moment and leaves its lanes empty, but picks the phase with the most waiting vehicles at only ~60% of its switches. I added a logit term `c·(u_q − mean u)`, where `u_q` is the approximate number of cars waiting for phase q (stop-line density in cars, plus half-weighted upstream lanes, shared lane split 65/35 through/left). It is built from 3 repurposed first-layer units (Hadamard contrasts of u), 3 repurposed second-layer pass-through units, their W3 columns, a b3 correction and 19 b2 mean-shift compensations. All values set by construction.\n\n**Parameters changed:** 371 (the cap).\n\n**Simulator calls:** 8 of 10. Strength c = 0.7–1.5 gave 44.6; c = 2.5 collapsed at high demand (66.4) by holding busy phases; halving the upstream weights fixed that and gave the best result. Dev TTS of the delivered weights: 44.3 veh-h (low 34.3, nominal 44.4, high 54.1) vs 44.8 for the original, no leftover vehicles.\n\n**Test predictions:** low 34.4, nominal 44.6, high 54.6 veh-h.","ttft_ms":2642,"type":"result","duration_ms":609459,"uuid":"c8e5e3a1-d28b-41b5-81f7-1f19b4b2ebff","ttft_stream_ms":2016,"time_to_request_ms":75,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":3,"system_prompt":18,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":12,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":4,"tool_pool_refresh":3,"init_message":4,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":5,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":5,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":1,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":25,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":104,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"input_attachments_detail":{